From now onwards, it was forbidden to sing it.

4
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:14,680
The animals were taken aback.

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,960
>> Why?

6
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,840
cried Muriel.

7
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,239
>> It is no longer needed, comrade.

8
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:24,439
Beasts of England was the song of the rebellion, but the rebellion is now

9
00:00:24,439 --> 00:00:30,000
completed. The execution of the traitors this afternoon was the final act. The

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,039
enemy, both external and internal has been defeated. In Beasts of England, we

11
00:00:36,039 --> 00:00:40,199
expressed our longing for a better society in days to come, but that

12
00:00:40,199 --> 00:00:43,039
society has now been established.

13
00:00:43,039 --> 00:00:47,000
Clearly, this song has no longer any purpose.

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,159
Frightened though they were, some of the animals might possibly have protested,

15
00:00:52,159 --> 00:01:00,600
but at this moment, the sheep set up their usual bleating of Four legs good, two legs bad.

16
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:04,600
Which went on for several minutes and put an end to the discussion.

17
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,279
So, Beasts of England was heard no more.

18
00:01:08,279 --> 00:01:16,920
